-- Updated Libra entries — planet-specific
DELETE FROM kb_planet_in_sign WHERE sign = 'Libra';

INSERT INTO kb_planet_in_sign (planet, sign, summary, life_patterns, relationships, challenges, growth, book_references) VALUES

('Sun', 'Libra', 'Identity through partnership and balance', 'Your core self emerges in relationship to others. You define yourself by your ability to see multiple sides, mediate conflict, and create harmony. Identity feels incomplete without reflecting back through someone else''s eyes. Your sense of self strengthens when you''re appreciated for your fairness and charm.', 'You attract others easily and thrive when there''s genuine reciprocity and admiration. Partners feel balanced by your perspective. You''re most alive when collaborating on something beautiful or just. You may choose partners who feel like your missing piece—your other half.', 'Sun in fall here means you struggle to assert your core identity without seeking consensus first. You can lose yourself in making others comfortable. Standing alone in your truth feels destabilizing. You may swing between being too accommodating and suddenly rigid when your need for recognition explodes.', 'Own that a strong identity includes knowing what YOU want—not just what''s fair or balanced. Practice deciding before consulting. Your gift is seeing both sides; your work is choosing yourself. When you own your preferences unapologetically, you magnetize the right mirrors.', 'Liz Greene on the Sun in air signs; Dane Rudhyar on Libra solar individuality'),

('Moon', 'Libra', 'Emotional needs expressed through balance and connection', 'You need emotional harmony above all else. Conflict triggers internal shutdown; you soothe yourself by creating peace around you. Feelings come to you through reflection—you understand your own emotions better when discussing them with someone trusted. Affection and approval deeply stabilize you.', 'You''re the peacekeeper in relationships and expect partners to reciprocate emotional fairness. You feel secure when both people''s needs are heard equally. You attract emotionally literate, relationship-focused partners. Intimacy for you means being truly heard and understood—not just physically present.', 'You may suppress authentic anger to keep the peace, leading to sudden resentment or passive resistance. Emotional indecision paralyzed you—you can''t choose what you feel. You fear abandonment if you rock the boat. You may over-accommodate others'' feelings at the expense of your own needs.', 'Allow yourself to feel without immediately fixing or balancing. Your emotions are valid even if they''re not "fair." Practice naming what you need emotionally before considering the other person. When you honor your own feelings first, relationships deepen with real intimacy, not just surface harmony.', 'Liz Greene on the Moon in Libra; Demetra George on the Feminine Moon'),

('Mercury', 'Libra', 'Thinking style that weighs all perspectives and communicates with grace', 'Your mind naturally sees both sides of any question. You think through dialogue and debate—mental stimulation requires someone to bounce ideas off. You articulate beautifully, weighing words carefully for impact. Logic is balanced by social awareness; you consider how your words land emotionally.', 'You excel in partnerships that include intellectual exchange—you need a partner who can discuss, debate, and refine ideas with you. Conversation is foreplay for you. You communicate diplomatically, finding the language that honors all viewpoints. Others seek you out for fair, balanced advice.', 'Your gift for seeing both sides can paralyze decision-making—you get stuck weighing pros and cons endlessly. You may avoid direct speech to keep things pleasant, leading to misunderstandings. Your thinking can be indecisive or superficial when you prioritize agreeableness over truth. You struggle with positions that require you to be "wrong."', 'Develop confidence in your own perspective before automatically balancing it. Being smart means sometimes choosing a side. Your strength is synthesis—take time to think deeply alone, then bring your integrated view to others. Decisive communication is more attractive than endless diplomacy.', 'Dane Rudhyar on Mercury in air signs; Debra Silverman on Libra communication'),

('Venus', 'Libra', 'Love style that is refined, reciprocal, and aesthetically conscious', 'Venus RULES Libra—this is your home planet, and you love with refinement, fairness, and genuine consideration. You seek partnership as your highest value. Beauty matters deeply to you; you''re drawn to aesthetically harmonious people and spaces. Love feels reciprocal and balanced—you give what you expect to receive.', 'You''re magnetic and charming; partners feel like they''ve found the "right one." You value loyalty and fidelity in return for your devotion. Romance is important—you want beautiful dates, thoughtful gestures, and genuine appreciation. You''re attracted to partners who respect equality and can engage you intellectually and sensually.', 'You may choose partners for their aesthetics or status rather than real compatibility, then feel trapped. You can be indecisive in love, comparing potential partners endlessly. You may avoid conflict so persistently that passion fades. You can become people-pleasing and lose yourself in making the relationship "pretty."', 'Choose partners based on values and shared vision, not just initial chemistry or appearance. Real intimacy requires honest conflict, not just harmony. Let your natural diplomacy soften rigidity, not eliminate authenticity. When you value yourself as highly as you value partnership, love becomes truly reciprocal.', 'Robert Hand on Venus in Libra; Liz Greene on Venus domicile themes'),

('Mars', 'Libra', 'Drive expressed through diplomacy rather than direct assertion', 'Mars is in detriment in Libra—your energy is indirect. You drive forward through persuasion, not force. Aggression feels wrong to you; you prefer negotiation and strategic partnership to dominate. Your action style is collaborative and considerate of others'' needs. You build alliances rather than conquer territories.', 'You succeed through teamwork and by making others want to help you. Conflict is exhausting and often avoided. You seduce rather than charge; you''re tactically brilliant at getting what you want while others feel heard. You''re drawn to partners who take action, and you provide balance and perspective.', 'Your drive can get stuck in indecision—you weigh the consequences so heavily you lose momentum. Anger comes out as coldness or passive resistance rather than direct communication. You can build resentment by never directly fighting for what you want. You may appear unmotivated when actually you''re just conflict-averse.', 'Channel your drive through genuine partnership and social impact. Your strength isn''t lone wolf action—it''s rallying others to a fair cause. Practice direct assertion without needing to soften it with "both sides are valid." Passive action is still action; choose it consciously, not from fear.', 'Steven Forrest on Mars in air signs; Liz Greene on Mars detriment'),

('Jupiter', 'Libra', 'Growth through connection, shared vision, and expanding your network', 'Jupiter in Libra brings luck through partnership and your ability to see potential in others. Growth comes from building bridges, networks, and collaborative ventures. You''re optimistic about human nature and believe in mutual benefit. Your generosity attracts abundance—people want to work with and support you.', 'You succeed in relationships, business partnerships, and group endeavors. Your faith in fairness and justice opens doors. Others feel expanded and more hopeful around you. Travel, culture, and meeting diverse people brings joy. You''re fortunate in love when you choose consciously rather than impulsively.', 'Optimism can become naïveté—you may over-trust others'' good intentions. Expansion through too many partnerships scattered your focus; you need clear boundaries. You can be gullible about people''s motives. Excessive people-pleasing for the sake of harmony can limit your authentic growth.', 'Your gift for seeing potential in others is powerful; extend it to yourself too. Trust your judgment about character, but verify through experience. Build a few deep, reciprocal partnerships rather than many shallow ones. Expansion happens when you combine your optimism with discernment.', 'Liz Greene on Jupiter in Libra; Dane Rudhyar on Jupiter luck and partnership'),

('Saturn', 'Libra', 'Discipline and life lessons through fairness, structure, and commitment', 'Saturn is EXALTED in Libra—your greatest strength. You naturally understand consequences, social responsibility, and the structure fairness requires. You discipline yourself through principles and the desire to do right by others. Your maturity comes from building equitable systems. You have natural authority in creating just environments.', 'You''re reliable, fair-minded, and people trust your judgment in disputes. You commit seriously to relationships and honor your agreements. Others respect your integrity. You succeed in mediation, law, diplomacy, and any role requiring impartial assessment. You build lasting partnerships based on mutual respect and clear agreements.', 'You can be overly rigid about fairness, making you seem cold. Fear of making the wrong call can paralyze you. You may have learned that love is conditional on being "good" or fair. Early relationships may have felt emotionally distant despite surface politeness. You can take others'' emotions as your burden.', 'Your superpower is creating fair structures that actually work. Use your natural authority to set boundaries clearly and kindly. Understand that true fairness sometimes requires imperfection or choosing a side. Let your integrity include self-care and self-worth, not just duty to others.', 'Liz Greene on Saturn exalted; Demetra George on Saturn''s gifts in Libra'),

('Uranus', 'Libra', 'Generational rebellion through questioning fairness and redefining relationships', 'Uranus in Libra (1968-1975) brought your generation to revolutionize partnership, justice, and aesthetics. Your generation questioned traditional relationship hierarchies and demanded equality. You''re drawn to unconventional approaches to love, partnership, and beauty. You rebel against passive acceptance of unjust systems.', 'You innovate in relationships—open partnerships, non-traditional family structures, and partnerships based on mutual growth appeal to you. You''re drawn to partners who challenge social norms with you. You build communities around shared ideals. You''re an advocate for equality and reform in your social sphere.', 'Your desire for radical change can seem chaotic to more traditional people. You may sabotage good relationships if they feel too conventional. Idealism about fairness can make you judgmental of those with different values. You may resist commitment if it feels like loss of freedom.', 'Channel your revolutionary spirit into real structural change, not just rebellion for its own sake. Your generation''s gift for reimagining partnership is powerful; refine it with commitment. Balance your need for freedom with genuine interdependence. Question traditions consciously, not reactively.', 'Stephen Forrest on Uranus in Libra generation; Dane Rudhyar on Uranus as revolutionary principle'),

('Neptune', 'Libra', 'Generational dreams of harmony, unity, and aesthetic transcendence', 'Neptune in Libra (1942-1956) dreamed of a world united by beauty, harmony, and fair principles. Your generation spiritualized partnership and equality. You''re drawn to ideals of peace and see the world through aesthetic and spiritual values. You seek transcendence through connection and creativity.', 'You create beauty and inspire others toward peace and harmony. You''re drawn to spirituality that emphasizes unity and shared consciousness. Partnerships feel destined if they seem to align with higher purpose. You excel in the arts, music, and visionary work that uplifts collective consciousness.', 'Idealism can become escapism—you may overlook real incompatibility for a beautiful dream. You can be vague about boundaries, merging with partners or groups without discernment. Your dreams of perfect harmony may not survive contact with real conflict. You''re vulnerable to being disappointed by partners who don''t match your spiritual ideals.', 'Ground your beautiful visions in practical reality. Use your spiritual sensitivity to perceive truth, not to escape difficulty. Healthy spirituality includes clear boundaries and honest self-awareness. Your gift is showing others the transcendent possibilities of harmony; live them authentically.', 'Liz Greene on Neptune in Libra; Dane Rudhyar on Neptune''s spiritual dimension'),

('Pluto', 'Libra', 'Generational transformation of power, partnership, and social justice', 'Pluto in Libra (1971-1984) brought your generation to transform power dynamics in partnership, transform concepts of fairness, and rebuild relationship structures. You instinctively question who holds power and how. You''re drawn to deep psychological work on relationships. You understand that real partnership requires facing shadow sides.', 'You''re catalysts for transformation in your relationships and communities. You see beneath surface politeness to real dynamics. You excel in psychology, investigation, and work that reveals hidden truths about power. Your partnerships are intense and transformative for both people. You''re unafraid of deep emotional and psychological work.', 'Your focus on power dynamics can make you suspicious or paranoid about relationships. You may be drawn to relationships that recreate old power struggles so you can transform them. Intensity can feel destructive to those seeking simple harmony. You may use emotional depth as a weapon or control mechanism.', 'Your superpower is seeing and transforming hidden dynamics. Use this for healing, not manipulation. Real power comes from honest self-awareness, not controlling others. Channel your intensity into collaborative transformation that serves everyone''s growth. When you integrate your own shadow, you help others do the same.', 'Donna Cunningham on Pluto in Libra; Liz Greene on Pluto''s transformative power');
